            <ArticleTitle>Prevention of complications in surgical management of back pain and sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Accurate diagnosis of lumbar disc disease requires a thorough examination. Appropriate neurodiagnostic studies are required to confirm the suspected diagnosis. Other diagnoses should be considered prior to surgery, especially when there is a lack of correlation between the history, physical examination, or radiologic investigation. Proper surgical techniques should also help in preventing complications and are further discussed in this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
